3.2. Target detection based on M1 LIDAR
3.2.1. Preprocessing of LIDAR point cloud
LIDAR is often disturbed and affected by the surrounding environment when collecting point cloud, and these unprocessed data are directly used for target detection may significantly reduce the speed and accuracy of detection. Therefore, it is necessary to select an effective point cloud detection range and streamline the point cloud. We utilizes point cloud downsampling and ground point removal techniques for preprocessing of the point cloud. Since LIDAR generates dense scanning data every second, resulting in a large number of highly similar point cloud in the overlapping area, which significantly increases the memory space, We uses the Voxel Grid filter for point cloud simplification, which can not only reduce the point cloud, but also maintain the shape characteristics of the point cloud. The core principle of the Voxel Grid filter is 3D voxelization grid, in which the input point cloud is divided into multiple voxels, and all points within the voxel are approximately represented by calculating the center of gravity of all points inside each voxel. This way of processing simplifies the point cloud, reduces redundant information, and helps to eliminate noise and outliers. The formula is as follows:
