5. CONCLUSION
We introduces the pedestrian detection method of LIDAR and camera fusion from three aspects: visual target detection algorithm, LIDAR target detection algorithm, and LIDAR and camera information fusion. Experiments involving joint calibration, point cloud preprocessing, and sensor fusion were conducted in a campus setting using the M1 solid-state LIDAR, Sen Yun smart camera, and a modified wheelchair trolley. Experimental results show that the accuracy of vision detection is 87.7%, the accuracy of LIDAR detection is 80.5%, and the accuracy of sensor fusion detection is 85.6%. Although the camera sensor detection rate is slightly higher than the sensor fusion detection rate, the camera sensor only in normal light with real-time, in dark light conditions the camera sensor does not have real-time easy to target leakage problem. Aiming at the above problems, We will further improve the visual target detection algorithm, so that it can have detection real-time in dark light conditions, in order to more accurately data fusion with LIDAR.
